1
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:06,319
We all know how it goes one day we're born one day we die.
我们都知道这套过程：有一天出生，有一天死去。

2
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:09,679
Everything that happens in between we know and understand.
发生在两者之间的事情，我们知道，也理解。

3
00:00:09,679 --> 00:00:14,799
But everything that happened before and will happen after we know nothing about.
但之前发生的一切，以及之后将发生的一切，我们一无所知。

4
00:00:14,799 --> 00:00:21,359
As a result it's really difficult to say what exactly the meaning or importance for us being here is.
因此，很难说我们身处这里究竟有什么意义或重要性。

5
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:27,599
If we can't tell how we came or where we came from how can we know why we're here.
如果说不清我们是如何、从哪里来的，又怎么知道我们为什么在这里？

6
00:00:27,599 --> 00:00:32,480
In the same vein if we don't know where we're going or what we're going to become.
同样，如果不知道我们将走向何方、变成什么，

7
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:36,719
How can we tell if any of our present actions have any significance at all.
又怎么判断现在的任何行动究竟有没有意义？

8
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:42,950
It is this uncertainty of both our collective pasts and futures that has allowed the question what is the meaning of life.
正是对我们共同的过去和未来的这种不确定，让“人生的意义是什么”这个问题，

9
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:46,160
To plague humanity ever since we became sentient.
自人类有意识以来就一直困扰着我们。

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:50,079
We've never been able to objectively answer this question as a species.
作为一个物种，我们从未能客观地回答这个问题。

11
00:00:50,079 --> 00:00:56,800
However a lot of us have found comfort in many different ideologies to at least subdue the anxiety that it causes.
不过，很多人在各种思想体系里找到了安慰，至少能压下这个问题带来的焦虑。

12
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:01,440
In many different religions a deity made the entire universe put us all in it.
在许多宗教的说法里，一位神创造了整个宇宙，把我们放进其中，

13
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:06,720
And whatever we do on this earth will be used to determine when and how we spend eternity afterwards.
而我们在地球上所做的一切，将被用来决定我们之后何时、以何种方式度过永恒。

14
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:12,320
For some others the meaning of life is the love we share with friends family and our loved ones.
对另一些人，人生的意义，是我们与朋友、家人、所爱之人分享的爱。

15
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:16,479
Some others believe the existence of life in itself is what makes it worth living.
还有人认为，生命本身的存在，就让它值得活下去。

16
00:01:16,479 --> 00:01:20,240
But for nihilists life is meaningless.
但对于虚无主义者，生命是没有意义的。

17
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:31,910
All action suffering emotions both good and bad are entirely senseless and meaningless this is nihilism the belief in nothing.
所有行动、痛苦、好的坏的情绪，全都毫无意义；这就是虚无主义，相信虚无。

18
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:36,479
At some point in our lives many of us have been faced with nihilistic thoughts.
人生中的某个时刻，我们很多人都曾面对过虚无主义式的想法。

19
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:42,789
We're hit by a strong sense of purposelessness like our lives have no meaning and we have no intrinsic value.
一种强烈的无目的感向我们袭来，好像人生毫无意义，自己也没有内在价值。

20
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:49,109
Usually this happens when we begin to question our old beliefs but also just before we get new ones to hold on to.
这通常发生在开始质疑旧信念，却还没有新的信念可依靠的时候。

21
00:01:49,119 --> 00:01:52,000
It's in that phase where you're growing out of your parents beliefs.
那是你逐渐摆脱父母信念的阶段，

22
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,030
Learning new things getting new experiences and forming your own views about the world.
学习新东西、获得新经历，形成自己对世界的看法。

23
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:03,119
And usually all of these thoughts begin with one simple question why.
而通常，这些想法都始于一个简单的问题：为什么？

24
00:02:03,119 --> 00:02:08,800
A three lettered monoselabic word that's capable of making anything and everything that feels like the rock of your foundation.
这个由三个字母组成的“monoselabic”词，有能力让那些似乎是你坚实根基的一切，

25
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,520
Start to become slippery like quicksand.
开始像流沙一样变得滑动不稳，

26
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:18,160
Dragging you into the misery that maybe just maybe your whole life hasn't been what you thought it was.
把你拖入痛苦：也许，仅仅也许，你整个人生并不是自己以为的样子。

27
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:23,920
Just pause and take a moment to think about your core values and just ask the question why.
暂停一下，花点时间想想你的核心价值观，就问一句：为什么？

28
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:29,120
Why do you believe those things where did they come from who did they come from.
你为什么相信那些事？它们从哪里来？从谁那里来？

29
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:33,750
Keep asking and eventually you'll arrive at a point where there's no longer an answer.
继续追问，最终会来到一个再也没有答案的地方。

30
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:43,559
You'll arrive at nothing all the religions of the world all of our scientific discovery but yet the question why is one that we still cannot answer.
你会走到虚无：世界所有的宗教、我们所有的科学发现，可“为什么”这个问题，仍然无法回答。

31
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:54,480
And so for the nihilist it is at this point that they come to the conclusion that there is no why there is no answer there's simply nothing.
因此，对虚无主义者来说，正是在这里，他们得出结论：没有为什么，没有答案，只有虚无。

32
00:02:54,480 --> 00:03:00,869
As alan watts once wrote life is nothing more than a trip from the maternity ward to the crematorium.
正如作者引用 Alan Watts 的话：“人生不过是从产房到火葬场的一程。”
